==== Upgrade from 23.05 to 24.10 ====
The kernel has grown, and doesn't fit in the 3MiB kernel partition anymore. To solve that the 24.10 image has a 5MiB kernel partition size, but that means you can't use sysupgrade to get 24.10 flashed, so you'll have to install it manually, using zyxel_p-2812hnu-f1-initramfs-kernel.bin.

Connect to the serial port of your P-2812HNU-F1, and reboot it. Check the version of u-boot. As far as I know the only u-boot for this box which can handle an (extracted) uImage size up to 16MiB, can be found in a download link on the end of [[https://forum.openwrt.org/t/zyxel-p2812hnu-f1-u-boot/100281/8|this forum thread]]. It shows version '**U-Boot 2013.10-openwrt5 (Jul 06 2021 - 10:04:01) P-2812HNU-Fx**'.
If you don't have that, update your uboot. The //U-Boot bootlog// shown below is an old one and should be updated before installing v24.10.0.
=== Update u-boot ===
Setup your tftp server and client side addresses as described above, and execute
<code>
tftpboot openwrt-lantiq-p2812hnufx_nandtpl-u-boot-16M-patch.img
</code>
output:
<code>
ltq_phy: addr 0, link 1, speed 100, duplex 1
ltq_phy: addr 1, link 0, speed 10, duplex 0
ltq_phy: addr 17, link 0, speed 100, duplex 0
ltq_phy: addr 19, link 0, speed 100, duplex 0
ltq_phy: addr 5, link 0, speed 10, duplex 0
Using ltq-eth device
TFTP from server 192.168.1.2; our IP address is 192.168.1.1
Filename 'openwrt-lantiq-p2812hnufx_nandtpl-u-boot-16M-patch.img'.
Load address: 0x81000000
Loading: ################
done
Bytes transferred = 231813 (38985 hex)
</code>
Then execute:
<code>
nand erase 0 $filesize && nand write $fileaddr 0 $filesize
</code>
output:
<code>
NAND write: device 0 offset 0x0, size 0x38985
 231813 bytes written: OK
</code>
Now powercycle the box. It should show u-boot '**U-Boot 2013.10-openwrt5 (Jul 06 2021 - 10:04:01) P-2812HNU-Fx**'.
=== Change u-boot environment ===
You'll have to tell u-boot to load a bigger image:
<code>
setenv nboot 'nand read 0x81000000 0x60000 0x500000; bootm 0x81000000' 
setenv bootcmd 'run nboot'
saveenv
</code>
=== Upload initramfs-kernel ===
Download zyxel_p-2812hnu-f1-initramfs-kernel.bin from the OpenWrt download server. 
Setup your tftp server and client side addresses as described above, and execute
<code>
tftpboot zyxel_p-2812hnu-f1-initramfs-kernel.bin
bootm $fileaddr
</code>
The box should now boot the initramfs-kernel, and when done, you should be able to access the router using it's webinterface.
Download zyxel_p-2812hnu-f1-squashfs-sysupgrade.bin from the OpenWrt download server, and upload it to the router via
*System->Backup/Flash firmware->Flash new firmware image*.

After uploading, the box reboots, and should be running OpenWrt 24.10 from flash.
=== Restore settings ===
If you were running 23.05, you can now restore your previously stored configuration. If you were running an older version, the stored configuration is not compatible. Do not upload it.
